  "reason": "The current best is config_031 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) at 0.715 accuracy, far ahead of all others. The evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder and avgpool as the aggregation method. However, the fusion method (concat vs. weighted) has only been tested with pca_n2000, where concat outperformed weighted. With the much richer scvi_n200 representation, the interaction between fusion strategy and encoder may differ. config_034 is a minimal single-variable perturbation of the best config (changing only fusion from concat to weighted), directly testing whether weighted fusion could further improve upon 0.715. With only 2 experiments remaining after this one, isolating one variable from the current best is the highest-value use of the next slot: if it improves, we find a new best; if not, we confirm concat is optimal and can spend the final 2 experiments on other axes (e.g., transformer aggregation or resnet50) with full confidence in the fusion choice."
}

